al:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. Replication was demonstrated normally, across a bounded disconnect with exact catch-up, and again after sequential node restarts. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity independently confirmed by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service, data, role, and replication state.","limitations":["An intermediate node2 probe reported @@read_only=0 despite simultaneously rejecting the write as read-only; subsequent global/session checks, restart recovery evidence, and the final application-user probe consistently show read_only=ON.","Lifecycle snapshots are generic and do not independently inspect database rows, grants, or the export; those outcomes rely on the executor's captured command outputs."]}
